      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Seagoville Public Library began in 1942 with just 85 books, grew through Lions Club support, and moved to its current site in 1975.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20,
        21,
        22,
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://communityhistoryarchives.com/places/seagoville-public-library/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "During World War II, Seagoville housed a federal reformatory that served as an internment camp for up to 647 enemy aliens and women of Japanese and German ancestry.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28,
        29,
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seagoville%2C_Texas",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "NBA star LaMarcus Aldridge and NFL player Antonio Wilson both grew up in Seagoville, while actor Chill Wills was born and raised there.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
